["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/act", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The vulnerability requires attention from the organization's internal, supervisory-level and leadership-level individuals. Necessary actions include requesting assistance or information about the vulnerability, as well as publishing a notification either internally and/or externally. Typically, internal groups would meet to determine the overall response and then execute agreed upon actions. CISA recommends remediating Act vulnerabilities as soon as possible.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType/expandedLicensing", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Person", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "An individual human being.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/performedBy", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ContactPointRelationshipType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "ContactPointRelationshipType", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipCompleteness/noAssertion", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "No assertion can be made about the completeness of the relationship.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/autonomous", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "Level 6 - Autonomous. The system is capable of modifying its intended domain of use or its goals without external intervention, control or oversight.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N4acb678f9e3745bd8bb02a79dc03d7b8", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:Nd5e83d2133504762af1e2bfa7279a2a2", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/modifiedTime", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "modifiedTime", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/scope", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Nb0650bf52bef4fe6b20f66471dd5874a", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#datatype", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Build/buildType", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A buildType is an IRI expressing the toolchain, platform, or infrastructure that\nthe build was invoked on.\n\nThe buildType is used to interpret the meaning of other build parameters by\ndefining the \"type\" of build; if the same buildType is seen in different Build\nelements, it means they are the same kind of build, but difference instances\nand possible with different configurations.\n\nIf you are not using a well-known buildType, it should be namespaced to a\ndomain you own to prevent conflicts with other buildType IRIs.\n\nExamples of a buildType can be:\n\n- A GitHub action workflow\n- A step in a GitHub actions pipeline\n- An invocation of a compiler or other tool\n- A script that orchestrates builds at a higher level\n\nKeep in mind that builds can be \"nested\" using the ancestorOf relationship.\n\nIf the buildType IRI is not recognized, it is still possible to inspect other\nproperties of the build, but it may not be possible to derive deeper meaning\nfrom them.\n\nFor more information, see the SLSA definition of buildType.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nbf8a9d0423b441969d5440a092d5dce4", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount", "1", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasDeclaredLicense", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/verificationMethod", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "verificationMethod refers to the specific approach used to confirm that a (lower level) requirement or implemented system element complies with its higher level requirement.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/builtTime", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "Specifies the time an artifact was built.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N4373bcd1457c4ea98f02cab3d17a149f", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount", "1", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/decisionType", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "Provide the enumeration of possible decisions in the\nStakeholder-Specific Vulnerability Categorization (SSVC) decision tree <https://www.cisa.gov/stakeholder-specific-vulnerability-categorization-ssvc>.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N586a159f4d6d4ee99ca7b48391aa4528", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N36f65fd90e25412f947fa3d21f2ba8cf", "localId", "", ""]
