["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "A reference to a Vulnerability Exploitability eXchange (VEX) statement which provides information on whether a product is impacted by a specific vulnerability in an included package and, if affected, whether there are actions recommended to remediate. See also NTIA VEX one-page summary <https://ntia.gov/files/ntia/publications/vex_one-page_summary.pdf>.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/CustomLicense", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A CustomLicense represents a License that is not listed on the\nSPDX License List <https://spdx.org/licenses>,\nand is therefore defined by an SPDX data creator.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/BoundaryDefinitionAction", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "Boundaries can be physical or abstract. This is the act of defining the boundaries.\n\nRelationship:\n\nFor each BoundaryDefinitionAction there is one and only one /Core/Relationship class or subclass with the relationshipType of createdBy on the to and a /Core/Agent class or subclass on the from.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
