["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/issn", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "International Standard Serial Number (ISSN) <https://www.issn.org/understanding-the-issn/what-is-an-issn/> is an eight-digit identifier for serial publications and other continuing resources standardized by ISO 3297 <https://www.iso.org/standard/84536.html>. It consists of two groups of four digits separated by a hyphen, where the final character is a check digit that may be an \"X\". The hyphen is retained when the identifier is stored electronically to maintain the standard 9-character string format (e.g., 1464-3693). The ISSN is media-specific; the same journal title may be assigned different identifiers for its physical and digital versions.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/AnnotationType/other", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Used to store extra information about an Element which is not part of a review (e.g. extra information provided during the creation of the Element).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/assistiveAutomation", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Level 1 - Assistive automation. The system assists an operator.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/forPickupLocation", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "This is the designated location for pickup of an item.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
