["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SimpleLicensing/customIdToLicense", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "Within a license expression, references can be made to a custom license or a\ncustom license addition.\n\nThe License Expression syntax\ndictates any reference starting with a\n\"LicenseRef-\" or \"AdditionRef-\" refers to license or addition text not found in\nthe official SPDX License List <https://spdx.org/licenses/>.\n\nThe key for the ElementMap is the string used in the license expression\nand the elementValue is target Element, which must be a CustomLicense,\nCustomLicenseAddition, or SimpleLicensingText.\n\nThe key for the ElementMap shall be matched against the license expression\nin a case-insensitive manner.\nThis is required because the entire license expression string is itself\ncase-insensitive.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/republishedBy", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Designates a from Vulnerability's details were tracked, aggregated, and/or enriched to improve context (i.e. NVD) by each to Agent.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/TestProcess", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Test Process defines the testing process for an element.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
