["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isil", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "International Standard Identifier for Libraries and Related Organizations (ISIL) <https://slks.dk/english/work-areas/libraries-and-literature/library-standards/isil/> is a unique alphanumeric code for identifying libraries, archives, museums, and related organizations standardized by ISO 15511 <https://www.iso.org/standard/77849.html>. It consists of a prefix\u2014which may be an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code or a non-country code assigned by the ISIL Registration Authority\u2014followed by a unit identifier, totaling up to 16 characters (e.g., FI-Sipoo-S\u00f6 or ZDB-1-SBD). Valid symbols include any alphanumeric character, solidus (/), hyphen-minus (-), or colon.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/LicenseAddition", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/probability", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "The probability score between 0 and 1 (0 and 100%) estimating the likelihood of\nexploitation in the wild in the next 30 days (following score publication).\nThe definition follows \"epss\" in\nEPSS Data <https://www.first.org/epss/data_stats>.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
