["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RoleRelationship", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "RoleRelationship is a concrete subclass of Relationship that captures the connection between an entities (such as a person, organization, tool, or component) and the specific position, function, or responsibility it fulfills. This relationship type is used when documenting roles that are not implicitly defined by the SPDX document structure, allowing explicit modeling of organizational responsibilities, tooling involvement, or component functions across systems or contexts.\nRoleRelationship inherits the from and to properties from Relationship, where:\n\n- relationshipType = hasRoleIn.\n- from: The element to which the role is assigned (the role recipient).\n- to: The context, system, element or domain within which the role exists.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/CvssSeverityType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "CvssSeverityType", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType/core", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The element follows the Core profile specification.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/evaluationBasedOn", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "The evaluationBasedOn property represents the linkage to the particular RequirementVerification that serves as the foundation for generating an EvaluationResult. It connects the evaluation outcome to the defined process or activity that verified the requirement, enabling traceability and verification of the evaluation\u2019s basis. This linkage is critical in systems engineering to ensure that evaluation conclusions clearly reference the verified requirements and their verification methods, supporting auditability, compliance, and quality control.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N38b2aec4a0c34ab2980a968e33bb3bc4", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/from", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/demonstration", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Relationship", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A Relationship is a grouping of characteristics unique to an assertion\nthat one Element is related to one or more other Elements in some way.\n\nTo explicitly assert that no such relationships exist, the to property\nshall contain the NoneElement individual and no other elements.\n\nA relationship that contains NoneElement and additional elements in the to\nproperty is not valid.\n\nTo explicitly assert that no assertions are being made regarding the\nexistence of such relationships, the to property shall contain the\nNoAssertionElement individual.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/trainingEnergyConsumption", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "Energy consumed when training the AI model that is\nbeing used in the AI system.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
